# VPS: /etc/iptables/rules.v4 excerpt (nat table).
# Tailnet clients (Tailscale CGNAT range) going into the tunnel are rewritten to a dedicated
# address, so home can route replies AND tell them apart from the VPS itself.
# Tailscale's own subnet-route SNAT must be disabled, or it rewrites first.
*nat
-A POSTROUTING -s <TAILNET_CGNAT_RANGE> -o <TUNNEL_IFACE> -j SNAT --to-source <TAILNET_SNAT_ADDR>
COMMIT

# Also on the VPS: net.ipv4.ip_forward=1, FORWARD accepts between tailscale0 and the
# tunnel interface, and filter-table allows for web + tunnel ports placed ABOVE the
# cloud image's default REJECT rule.
